    {
      "title": "One Nation’s AI video is vile and tired – but the ensloppification of Australian politics doesn’t stop there",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/09/one-nations-ai-video-is-vile-and-tired-but-the-ensloppification-of-australian-politics-doesnt-stop-there-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>The inflammatory clip shows the wild west of online politicking created by unrestricted access to AI – and why watchdogs need more powers to do something about it</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>One Nation’s new AI-generated campaign video is a new low – even for them.</p><p>The video – reportedly played <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/03/one-nation-victoria-campaign-launch-abolish-first-nations-treaty-legalise-pepper-spray-ntwnfb\">at the party’s Victorian campaign launch</a> over the weekend – is an AI-generated collection of racist tropes, depicting a man who appears to be African brandishing a machete, an apparently Middle Eastern man with an explosive vest, a South Asian man in a turban talking about “mass migration” and an Indigenous elder talking about people receiving “money … on the basis of need, not identity”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/09/one-nations-ai-video-is-vile-and-tired-but-the-ensloppification-of-australian-politics-doesnt-stop-there-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T14:00:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bachelor star Sam Wood denied bail as police allege he choked wife until she ‘thought she would die’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/sam-wood-bachelor-bail-court-custody-domestic-violence-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Court hears police attended Wood’s Victorian home over a similar allegation about three years ago, but Snezana Wood had not complained then out of ‘fear of retribution’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The wife of former Bachelor star Sam Wood told police she “thought she was going to die” after he allegedly choked and assaulted her, a Queensland court heard on Thursday.<br /><br />\n The court also heard that police in Victoria had attended Wood’s home in relation to a similar incident about three years ago, but that his wife, Snezana Wood, had not wanted to make a complaint at that time out of “fear of retribution”.</p><p>Sam Wood, a 46-year-old wellness influencer from Melbourne, was denied bail in a Queensland court on Thursday and will be held in custody indefinitely awaiting trial, after police argued his behaviour was “escalating” and that he posed an unacceptable risk.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/sam-wood-bachelor-bail-court-custody-domestic-violence-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T05:58:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "NSW police commissioner made last-minute bid to hold closed-door hearings into Sydney anti-Herzog protest",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/nsw-police-commissioner-lanyon-bid-stop-public-inquiry-sydney-anti-herzog-protest-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Police watchdog says Mal Lanyon’s timing in raising the issue was ‘regrettable’ and led to delays</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The New South Wales police commissioner made a last-minute bid to hold hearings into <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/feb/14/inside-the-chaos-at-sydney-anti-herzog-protest-ntwnfb\">Sydney’s anti-Herzog protest</a> behind closed doors, delaying the inquiry, the police watchdog has revealed.</p><p>The Law Enforcement Conduct Commission (Lecc) has said that its inquiry into the February protest at Sydney’s town hall, launched after widespread allegations of police brutality, would go ahead this month with a mix of public and private examinations, saying the timing of issues raised by police commissioner, Mal Lanyon, was “regrettable”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/nsw-police-commissioner-lanyon-bid-stop-public-inquiry-sydney-anti-herzog-protest-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T05:30:47"
    }
